"make fastcheck"
	builds the library and the sample programs and does a simple
	self check: msz sends mrz.c, msz.c and the mrz and msz programs
	themselves to mrz over a named pipe, and the received files are
	compared with the originals.  It prints "the test failed" and
	exits with an error if a file differs.
	This test just covers basic ZMODEM functionality.

	The receiver may log a line like "Got ERROR" during the test.
	That is the protocol recovering from a duplicated header at
	the start of the session; the test still passes.

"make check"
	does not run any tests at the moment.

"make vcheck", "make oldcheck-local" and the dejagnu tests in the
testsuite directory
	are left over from lrzsz and do not work: check.lrzsz and the
	.exp files run the lrz and lsz programs with command line
	options that mrz and msz do not have, and some of them need
	other ZMODEM implementations (omen.sz, omen.rz, zmtx, zmrx).
